# Crease — daily growth engine. Installed at /etc/cron.d/crease-growth.
#
# This droplet keeps per-project crons in /etc/cron.d/, NOT in root's user
# crontab. Never pipe to `crontab -` here: it clobbers the other five sites'
# jobs (nemo-growth, nemo-seo, rentmap-growth, rentmap-scrape, rentmap-*).
#
# CRON_TZ matters. The droplet runs UTC, and without it the job drifts an hour
# at every daylight-saving change and stops being "the morning run".
#
# 05:20 America/New_York, chosen against the neighbours rather than for itself:
# rentmap-growth runs at 05:00 ET and nemo-growth at 06:00 ET, and this box has
# roughly 800MB free. Three Python engines and a model call at the same minute
# is how a 1GB box OOM-kills a live site.
#
# Credentials are NOT sourced here — growth_run.sh reads growth.env itself,
# because that file holds values a shell `.` in a cron line would mangle.
CRON_TZ=America/New_York
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin

20 5 * * * root cd /root/Crease-growth && ./growth_run.sh daily --email divinejdavis@gmail.com >> /var/log/crease-growth.log 2>&1

# Watchdog, from its own entry so it survives the engine failing. If the 05:20
# run stops happening the failure mode is an empty inbox, which looks exactly
# like a quiet week. This makes silence loud: it reports on the state the
# morning run left behind, whatever that state is.
40 11 * * * root cd /root/Crease-growth && python3 growth_daily.py report --email divinejdavis@gmail.com >> /var/log/crease-growth.log 2>&1
